<tool id="recap_prok_module4_nr_analysis" name="RECAP-PROK NR Result Analysis" version="0.1.0" profile="25.1">
    <description>classify best NCBI NR hits for hypothetical proteins</description>
    <requirements>
        <requirement type="package" version="3.12">python</requirement>
        <requirement type="package" version="1.84">biopython</requirement>
        <requirement type="package" version="3.9.2">matplotlib</requirement>
    </requirements>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
python '$__tool_directory__/module4_nr_analysis.py'
  --reann '$reann_nr'
  --ref '$ref_nr'
  --out-best-reann '$reann_best'
  --out-best-ref '$ref_best'
  --out-summary '$summary'
  --out-pdf '$figure'
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <param name="reann_nr" type="data" format="tabular" label="Re-annotated hypothetical proteins: NCBI NR DIAMOND results"/>
        <param name="ref_nr" type="data" format="tabular" label="Reference-mapped hypothetical proteins: NCBI NR DIAMOND results"/>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="reann_best" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: re-annotated best NR hits"/>
        <data name="ref_best" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: reference-mapped best NR hits"/>
        <data name="summary" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: NR classification summary"/>
        <data name="figure" format="pdf" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: NR classification figure"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test>
            <param name="reann_nr" value="Galaxy21-[Diamond on dataset 8_ Blast Tabular].tabular"/>
            <param name="ref_nr" value="Galaxy22-[Diamond on dataset 7_ Blast Tabular].tabular"/>
            <output name="reann_best">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="qseqid"/>
                    <has_text text="nr_class"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="ref_best">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="qseqid"/>
                    <has_text text="nr_class"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="summary">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="Dataset"/>
                    <has_text text="Strict hypothetical/unclassified"/>
                    <has_text text="Putative functional evidence"/>
                    <has_text text="Clear functional annotation"/>
                    <has_text text="Re-annotated&#x9;Strict hypothetical/unclassified&#x9;1&#x9;33.33"/>
                    <has_text text="Re-annotated&#x9;Putative functional evidence&#x9;1&#x9;33.33"/>
                    <has_text text="Re-annotated&#x9;Clear functional annotation&#x9;1&#x9;33.33"/>
                    <has_text text="Reference-mapped&#x9;Strict hypothetical/unclassified&#x9;1&#x9;25.00"/>
                    <has_text text="Reference-mapped&#x9;Putative functional evidence&#x9;1&#x9;25.00"/>
                    <has_text text="Reference-mapped&#x9;Clear functional annotation&#x9;2&#x9;50.00"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="figure">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_size value="10000" delta="10000"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[
Analyze Galaxy DIAMOND searches against NCBI NR.

Use BLAST tabular output without a header and select these fields in this exact order:

1. Query Seq-id (qseqid)
2. Subject Seq-id (sseqid)
3. Percentage identical (pident)
4. Query sequence length (qlen)
5. Subject sequence length (slen)
6. Alignment length (length)
7. Expect value (evalue)
8. Bit score (bitscore)
9. Subject title (stitle)

The tool selects the best hit for each query by highest bit score, with lowest
E-value as the tie-breaker, then classifies the NR title into strict hypothetical,
putative functional evidence, or clear functional annotation.
    ]]></help>
